WEBVTT

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:07.860
Seriously, working in
the middle of a tournament…

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:10.740
Done!

00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:14.840
Now for the presentation…

00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:19.900
[Save changes?]
[Yes] [No]

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:26.320
Hey, Mikoto!

00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:28.180
Oh crap!

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:30.880
Wake up or we'll be late!

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:32.120
I'm coming!

00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:04.640
[#06: Presentation]

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:06.240
[#06: Presentation]
Good morning.

00:02:07.940 --> 00:02:09.300
Stayed up late?

00:02:09.480 --> 00:02:12.180
Preparing materials for
the presentation took forever.

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:13.740
You sure you're okay?

00:02:14.020 --> 00:02:17.300
We've got work to do
outside of the presentation, you know.

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:19.300
Right, the tasting event!

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:23.220
I know you're tired from the tournament,
but we'll need all hands on deck now.

00:02:23.600 --> 00:02:26.880
Please! Why do you think they call us Badrymen?

00:02:27.140 --> 00:02:29.340
So… what's this tasting event, anyway?

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:31.160
This is getting old…

00:02:31.340 --> 00:02:36.340
I told you, the presentation's right after we see
the customers' reactions at the tasting event!

00:02:37.660 --> 00:02:43.280
Really? Can't you be a bit more
involved in your own project?

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:46.280
We gotta make it all count!

00:02:46.580 --> 00:02:47.080
Right.

00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:48.980
Hey, Shiratori.

00:02:49.700 --> 00:02:50.880
I need your help.

00:02:51.080 --> 00:02:51.960
Oh, sure.

00:02:52.300 --> 00:02:54.440
I'll need you too after you're done!

00:02:57.920 --> 00:02:59.900
Who's going to wear this thing?

00:02:59.900 --> 00:03:02.320
You, who else?

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:03.100
What?

00:03:03.270 --> 00:03:04.980
Go air it out on the rooftop for now.

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:08.280
There… we go!

00:03:08.740 --> 00:03:12.300
Wow, you badminton boys
have some great core strength!

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:14.020
I can't see where I'm going, though.

00:03:14.420 --> 00:03:16.520
Shiratori, I need a hand!

00:03:16.700 --> 00:03:17.040
Sure.

00:03:17.320 --> 00:03:18.900
Shiratori, I need you too.

00:03:18.900 --> 00:03:19.420
Sure.

00:03:19.520 --> 00:03:20.900
Shiratori!

00:03:20.960 --> 00:03:21.300
Coming!

00:03:21.460 --> 00:03:22.400
Shiratori!

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:23.120
Coming!

00:03:23.260 --> 00:03:24.720
Shiratori!

00:03:24.720 --> 00:03:26.200
C-Coming…!

00:03:28.880 --> 00:03:30.560
Is odd jobs all I'm good for…?

00:03:30.820 --> 00:03:32.780
Look at you, you busy bee!

00:03:33.320 --> 00:03:34.840
You want something from me too?

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:39.120
Ever heard of a "meeting"? You can't hold
an event without the Planning Department.

00:03:40.760 --> 00:03:43.520
Mikoto, let's run down the list of invited guests.

00:03:44.280 --> 00:03:48.520
I made a list of our best clients here,
but can you think of anyone else?

00:03:49.880 --> 00:03:51.500
Why not invite your parents?

00:03:51.640 --> 00:03:53.060
Oh, good idea.

00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:55.940
Let's invite Toya's parents too!

00:03:55.940 --> 00:03:58.040
Not my folks…

00:03:58.040 --> 00:03:59.180
Grow up!

00:03:59.500 --> 00:04:03.540
I heard Usuyama always invites his family.

00:04:03.980 --> 00:04:06.120
Oh, I didn't know he's married.

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:07.260
They even have a kid!

00:04:07.720 --> 00:04:10.960
He stopped playing badminton
after he got married.

00:04:11.660 --> 00:04:15.620
Back in high school, he rivaled
even Mitsuhoshi's Ibuki Sentaro.

00:04:15.800 --> 00:04:19.360
They even called them "Ibuki of the West"
and "Usuyama of the East."

00:04:20.020 --> 00:04:23.340
He was a regular contender
for the intercollegiate championship too.

00:04:23.480 --> 00:04:25.040
He was a big deal, then.

00:04:25.460 --> 00:04:30.140
His job rules his life now, though.
He never lets his guard down.

00:04:30.460 --> 00:04:33.840
Man, I also wanna get married!

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:36.160
Get married to whom?

00:04:37.240 --> 00:04:38.660
I sure wonder…

00:04:40.160 --> 00:04:42.320
Seems to be no issue with the ingredients.

00:04:43.060 --> 00:04:46.560
It should be alright to produce
a few for the tasting event.

00:04:46.940 --> 00:04:48.860
I'll get in touch with Production, then.

00:04:49.160 --> 00:04:50.140
Appreciate it.

00:04:52.280 --> 00:04:54.440
I'm impressed they made it this far.

00:05:08.080 --> 00:05:08.820
Alright.

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:12.160
That should be that for
the tasting event invitations.

00:05:12.700 --> 00:05:14.620
I hope they all come…

00:05:16.180 --> 00:05:18.820
Dude, you stained your suit!

00:05:19.080 --> 00:05:21.500
Oh, must have been
the curry udon from the other day.

00:05:21.710 --> 00:05:24.080
You gotta get it dry-cleaned.

00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:26.400
And what will I wear then?

00:05:26.400 --> 00:05:29.540
Wait, don't tell me you only have one suit?

00:05:30.420 --> 00:05:31.380
Why would I need more?

00:05:31.580 --> 00:05:36.120
You've gotta be kidding…
Suits are like a business card of the wearer.

00:05:41.560 --> 00:05:42.720
Alright then.

00:05:47.000 --> 00:05:51.800
Excuse me, could you help this lad find a suit?

00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:54.500
Of course, please come right in.

00:05:55.180 --> 00:05:57.080
Allow me to introduce our fabrics first.

00:05:57.680 --> 00:06:04.340
Our fabrics are made in three
countries: Italy, England, and Japan.

00:06:04.620 --> 00:06:07.920
The Italian fabrics are characterized by
their smooth texture, appearance,

00:06:08.080 --> 00:06:11.240
as well as the strong colors and their softness.

00:06:11.360 --> 00:06:16.480
British fabrics are thicker, appropriate
for the cold weather of the local climate.

00:06:16.480 --> 00:06:17.520
Similarly, Japanese fabrics are thick and durable.

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:20.260
- Now in Japanese, please…
- This fabric is typical of Owari
and western Aichi Prefecture…

00:06:35.500 --> 00:06:37.740
Please take a seat and wait just a moment.

00:06:38.900 --> 00:06:39.940
Hey, look!

00:06:40.640 --> 00:06:43.880
What do you think? Wanna have matching pins?

00:06:44.300 --> 00:06:46.000
Absolutely not.

00:06:46.100 --> 00:06:46.840
Naww…

00:06:48.100 --> 00:06:50.840
I didn't know buying a suit
could be so exhausting…

00:06:51.320 --> 00:06:54.800
How you dress can really
change the impression you give off,

00:06:54.800 --> 00:06:57.240
and hopefully even make your presentation go well.

00:06:57.400 --> 00:07:01.900
But I'm so glad Usuyama approved
Scallion Ginger Ale after all…

00:07:02.020 --> 00:07:05.120
Yeah, you wouldn't have gotten
this far without QA's cooperation.

00:07:05.280 --> 00:07:07.860
Usuyama was so harsh though!

00:07:08.440 --> 00:07:11.600
Now I get why you call QA "cops"…

00:07:11.860 --> 00:07:16.280
Being serious and stubborn is what
we love about him, after all, but…

00:07:16.960 --> 00:07:20.860
I do wish he was more honest with himself.

00:07:22.040 --> 00:07:25.840
It's obvious he's never gotten over badminton.

00:07:26.300 --> 00:07:29.650
Why else would he make up lame excuses
to come watch us at the tournament?

00:07:31.680 --> 00:07:34.360
Ah, your shirts are all creased again!

00:07:34.480 --> 00:07:35.340
Let them be.

00:07:36.200 --> 00:07:38.960
You think the tasting event will go well?

00:07:39.180 --> 00:07:39.920
Who knows.

00:07:40.100 --> 00:07:42.200
"Who knows"?
Is that all you've got to say?

00:07:42.520 --> 00:07:46.680
We've been working on this project as a team,
don't you wanna contribute somehow?

00:07:47.140 --> 00:07:52.700
The samples are ready.
What else can I do when I'm in QA?

00:07:53.000 --> 00:07:54.400
It's the feeling that counts…

00:07:55.860 --> 00:07:58.980
Unless something goes horribly wrong,
suppose it should go fine…

00:07:59.240 --> 00:08:00.340
Why shouldn't it go fine?

00:08:13.880 --> 00:08:16.140
What's this thing
we've got left in the warehouse?

00:08:16.360 --> 00:08:19.660
Hmm, aren't those the ingredients
for the tasting event?

00:08:19.880 --> 00:08:23.060
But we made so few samples,
how could anything be left over…

00:08:25.380 --> 00:08:27.980
Could you tell me more about this issue?

00:08:32.860 --> 00:08:35.600
Now we just wait for the drinks to arrive…

00:08:37.960 --> 00:08:39.640
Goes well with your eyes!

00:08:44.420 --> 00:08:46.260
And here are our drinks!

00:08:47.500 --> 00:08:49.200
What about Scallion Ginger Ale?

00:08:49.840 --> 00:08:52.640
I'm sorry, this was all I was given.

00:08:53.020 --> 00:08:55.240
What? That can't be…

00:08:55.240 --> 00:08:56.660
We've run into a problem.

00:08:57.940 --> 00:09:00.820
That's why we'll be
withholding Scallion Ginger Ale

00:09:01.500 --> 00:09:02.760
from today's tasting event.

00:09:07.840 --> 00:09:10.260
Withholding? But why?!

00:09:10.760 --> 00:09:17.720
It appears that some of the Scallion Ginger Ale
ingredients have been left over.

00:09:18.440 --> 00:09:23.340
We cannot ignore the possibility that
another product's ingredients were used instead.

00:09:24.240 --> 00:09:25.580
All this over a "possibility"?!

00:09:25.580 --> 00:09:29.540
Reducing that possibility
to 0 is what we do at QA.

00:09:30.160 --> 00:09:33.840
Therefore, I cannot risk Scallion Ginger Ale
being served at the tasting event.

00:09:33.840 --> 00:09:34.900
But we…

00:09:36.840 --> 00:09:38.640
But that's not certain yet, is it?

00:09:38.800 --> 00:09:41.780
Let's just say the possibility is extremely high.

00:09:41.780 --> 00:09:45.220
I'll go ask my colleagues if we can do something!

00:09:45.420 --> 00:09:49.120
And I'll go ask them to change
the order of the tasting event.

00:09:49.740 --> 00:09:51.640
Let's do whatever we can for now.

00:09:52.240 --> 00:09:55.020
Maybe they just ordered too much.

00:09:55.420 --> 00:09:56.800
Let's go check the order slips.

00:09:57.040 --> 00:10:00.560
Go on. We'll stall for time if we have to.

00:10:00.920 --> 00:10:01.860
Really, Ninosaka?

00:10:01.860 --> 00:10:04.260
Honestly I'll deserve a bonus after this.

00:10:06.020 --> 00:10:09.680
Let's send someone to check
the Tatebayashi warehouse in person.

00:10:09.880 --> 00:10:10.580
I'll go!

00:10:10.580 --> 00:10:11.140
No.

00:10:12.060 --> 00:10:12.900
I'll go.

00:10:14.520 --> 00:10:16.380
Why would you get involved here?

00:10:17.080 --> 00:10:21.980
I was helping with the project proposal. I don't
want this to leave a bad taste in my mouth.

00:10:22.540 --> 00:10:24.840
Okay! Then we'll leave that to you, Sota.

00:10:25.120 --> 00:10:26.020
I appreciate it.

00:10:27.420 --> 00:10:31.500
Excuse me! Where can I find the order slips
for the ingredients for Scallion Ginger Ale?

00:10:33.600 --> 00:10:35.460
It's an emergency, guys. We need the help.

00:10:35.780 --> 00:10:38.620
We've sent all the slips to accounting.

00:10:39.260 --> 00:10:40.360
Thank you!

00:10:41.240 --> 00:10:42.000
Order slips?

00:10:42.740 --> 00:10:44.600
We've put them all in the storage cabinet.

00:10:44.600 --> 00:10:46.600
Can you let us in?

00:10:48.400 --> 00:10:50.100
Come on, where are they?!

00:10:50.480 --> 00:10:53.320
Given the date, they should be here!

00:10:53.600 --> 00:10:55.340
Are you sure you put them here?

00:10:55.540 --> 00:11:00.360
Of course. It's where we put all
the order slips once we're done processing them.

00:11:01.260 --> 00:11:02.200
Is that really true?

00:11:03.460 --> 00:11:04.680
W-Why would I lie?

00:11:13.400 --> 00:11:14.700
Then what's all this?

00:11:14.700 --> 00:11:16.700
Looks like unorganized order slips to me.

00:11:16.920 --> 00:11:20.280
W-We've just been so busy recently!

00:11:22.520 --> 00:11:25.420
Please just don't tell my boss!

00:11:41.380 --> 00:11:42.960
Oh, Mrs. Saeki?

00:11:43.640 --> 00:11:45.760
So good to see you again!

00:11:46.500 --> 00:11:49.720
My, Mrs. Shiratori, you look as good as ever!

00:11:49.720 --> 00:11:51.120
Papa!

00:11:52.090 --> 00:11:52.950
Megumu.

00:11:53.320 --> 00:11:54.380
We're here!

00:11:54.740 --> 00:11:56.940
What's wrong, dear?

00:11:58.560 --> 00:12:00.060
Oh, no, everything's fine.

00:12:00.430 --> 00:12:03.510
The badminton team's drink,
what was it called again…

00:12:03.780 --> 00:12:05.200
Scallion Ginger Ale!

00:12:05.200 --> 00:12:08.060
That's it! Can't wait to try it, right?

00:12:08.060 --> 00:12:08.700
Yeah!

00:12:08.700 --> 00:12:10.140
How did you know about that?

00:12:10.740 --> 00:12:14.320
Because his papa was talking
about his job at home for a change.

00:12:14.680 --> 00:12:15.880
It kinda stuck out!

00:12:17.040 --> 00:12:18.220
I was…?

00:12:18.940 --> 00:12:25.540
Thank you all for coming to Sunlight
Beverage's tasting event today!

00:12:26.000 --> 00:12:31.480
Today, we're excited to have you try some
samples of drinks from our internal contest!

00:12:31.720 --> 00:12:36.400
They're coming to you fresh off
the production belt! Without further ado…

00:12:36.780 --> 00:12:39.260
Our first drink is…

00:12:40.300 --> 00:12:41.600
Ah, where are they?!

00:12:41.900 --> 00:12:44.300
Less talking, more looking.

00:12:44.500 --> 00:12:46.000
What do you think I'm doing?!

00:12:48.500 --> 00:12:49.360
Usuyama?!

00:12:49.760 --> 00:12:52.120
You don't have time to act surprised.

00:12:52.800 --> 00:12:54.420
Our second drink is…

00:12:54.420 --> 00:12:57.320
Orange Juice, Red Edition!

00:13:06.160 --> 00:13:07.260
This is it!

00:13:07.660 --> 00:13:09.100
Five bags, right?

00:13:09.320 --> 00:13:10.120
That's it.

00:13:10.340 --> 00:13:12.700
Couldn't have been an order error, then…

00:13:13.000 --> 00:13:15.680
Then what were those leftover ingredients?

00:13:17.240 --> 00:13:18.560
It's Sota!

00:13:18.880 --> 00:13:19.660
And?

00:13:20.120 --> 00:13:25.440
The bags in the warehouse looked similar,
but they're unrelated to Scallion Ginger Ale.

00:13:26.080 --> 00:13:29.000
It seems they brought them here by mistake.

00:13:30.220 --> 00:13:33.060
Okay. So there's nothing wrong
with our samples then.

00:13:33.680 --> 00:13:34.940
Head right back…

00:13:36.220 --> 00:13:39.360
What? All the trucks are busy?

00:13:39.800 --> 00:13:44.120
They got a sudden order
and sent their last trucks for it.

00:13:44.520 --> 00:13:46.920
Alright. Thanks for the help, Sota.

00:13:47.060 --> 00:13:48.560
After everything we've done…

00:13:54.660 --> 00:13:57.160
It's me. Got a minute?

00:13:58.420 --> 00:14:01.000
The next drink will be our last this event!

00:14:01.380 --> 00:14:03.860
Last but not least, let's try…

00:14:07.680 --> 00:14:15.060
L-Let's try to appreciate our lovely mascot,
the SunBeaver before our last drink!

00:14:15.620 --> 00:14:18.420
I'm not getting paid nearly enough for this!

00:14:20.720 --> 00:14:22.740
Stalling for time won't do squat for us now…

00:14:23.640 --> 00:14:26.680
What're you sulking for? We're not done yet.

00:14:26.940 --> 00:14:28.480
No, we're super done…

00:14:45.180 --> 00:14:46.020
Azuma?!

00:14:47.870 --> 00:14:50.290
The time has finally come!

00:14:50.290 --> 00:14:54.480
The crown jewel of our tasting event,
the Scallion Ginger Ale is here!

00:15:00.380 --> 00:15:02.460
It's so refreshing, goes right down!

00:15:02.460 --> 00:15:04.960
It smells a little of apples too!

00:15:14.380 --> 00:15:15.300
Liked my entrance?

00:15:15.400 --> 00:15:16.400
It was a lot to take in.

00:15:16.960 --> 00:15:19.440
Never thought I'd see you in a decorated truck.

00:15:19.760 --> 00:15:23.500
Never thought I'd see you working in Sales.

00:15:23.880 --> 00:15:24.900
You've got a point.

00:15:26.420 --> 00:15:27.400
So, um…

00:15:29.020 --> 00:15:30.660
You saved my ass today.

00:15:31.620 --> 00:15:33.660
Thanks, Azuma.

00:15:35.800 --> 00:15:37.560
You really did change, Mikoto.

00:15:38.020 --> 00:15:40.300
Like, you're more honest
about your feelings now.

00:15:40.300 --> 00:15:42.980
What? N-No, I'm not…

00:15:46.620 --> 00:15:49.400
I can play badminton at full strength again.

00:15:50.500 --> 00:15:55.160
I really did have fun playing with you.
Even if you were on the other side of the net.

00:15:56.120 --> 00:15:57.400
I had fun too.

00:15:59.040 --> 00:16:00.320
You won't beat me next time.

00:16:04.940 --> 00:16:05.920
Right back at you.

00:16:12.980 --> 00:16:13.660
Alright.

00:16:22.860 --> 00:16:26.200
Let's hear from our Sales Department next.

00:16:26.420 --> 00:16:27.340
Yes, sir.

00:16:29.320 --> 00:16:33.820
Today, I would like to introduce
Scallion Ginger Ale to you.

00:16:36.640 --> 00:16:39.160
You think Shiratori will manage?

00:16:39.160 --> 00:16:40.460
Really can't say.

00:16:40.460 --> 00:16:41.800
See ya.

00:16:42.280 --> 00:16:44.240
Don't you care how the presentation will go?

00:16:44.420 --> 00:16:46.480
I'm not paid to care.

00:16:46.880 --> 00:16:48.760
Gosh, Ninosaka never changes…

00:16:49.240 --> 00:16:53.900
Given how hard he was stalling for time,
I think he cares more than he lets on.

00:16:54.180 --> 00:16:55.580
You think so?

00:16:56.630 --> 00:17:00.750
But you gotta admit,
that was one heck of a truck.

00:17:04.120 --> 00:17:05.900
Sorry for the sudden order!

00:17:06.100 --> 00:17:07.440
Oh, no, it's no problem.

00:17:08.260 --> 00:17:10.030
If anything, the truck's a bit…

00:17:10.380 --> 00:17:13.440
Aren't our babies awesome?

00:17:15.920 --> 00:17:18.080
I… think I'm too young for "babies."

00:17:19.200 --> 00:17:22.520
That will be all.
Thank you for your attention.

00:17:22.800 --> 00:17:25.140
Sounds good to me!

00:17:25.440 --> 00:17:30.780
Indeed. I can certainly appreciate the novelty.

00:17:30.780 --> 00:17:32.920
Right? It'll stand out from…

00:17:32.920 --> 00:17:34.340
However.

00:17:34.720 --> 00:17:39.540
Novelty drinks hardly impress
our customers anymore.

00:17:39.700 --> 00:17:43.740
Well, but thinking outside of the box
is something our company has…

00:17:43.740 --> 00:17:47.560
"Our company" is carrying the lives
of many employees on its back.

00:17:47.560 --> 00:17:50.600
We cannot afford to underperform anymore.

00:17:51.060 --> 00:17:54.880
Of course, I understand that. Nevertheless…

00:17:55.120 --> 00:17:57.040
This isn't looking good for us, is it?

00:17:57.040 --> 00:17:59.220
The president crumbles under pressure.

00:17:59.220 --> 00:18:02.580
What our company needs
is focusing on our strengths!

00:18:02.700 --> 00:18:04.600
What good can novelty products do for us?

00:18:05.040 --> 00:18:10.440
According to the proposal, ramune bottles
will help with the first impression,

00:18:10.740 --> 00:18:14.120
but how do you even hope to obtain
pure glass bottles in this day and age?

00:18:15.460 --> 00:18:18.740
To answer your question, we've prepared
this document in advance.

00:18:23.420 --> 00:18:25.360
Takeda, what are you doing?

00:18:27.140 --> 00:18:29.820
This one isn't on me, Shiratori!

00:18:29.820 --> 00:18:31.560
The file is empty!

00:18:32.560 --> 00:18:33.680
That's impossible…

00:18:35.120 --> 00:18:35.880
But how?

00:18:37.320 --> 00:18:38.860
Whatever might be the issue?

00:18:38.860 --> 00:18:39.880
Oh, um…

00:18:45.340 --> 00:18:46.560
We're so screwed!

00:18:47.560 --> 00:18:49.740
Imagine they're all naked.

00:19:02.740 --> 00:19:04.840
Do you find this situation amusing?

00:19:04.840 --> 00:19:06.100
Wow, this really works…

00:19:07.300 --> 00:19:10.180
Allow me to explain instead.

00:19:10.460 --> 00:19:15.360
We've already discussed with the manufacturer
the prospect of pure glass ramune bottles.

00:19:15.920 --> 00:19:20.640
The use of returnable bottles will also reduce
CO2 emissions and energy consumption

00:19:20.640 --> 00:19:24.010
required for packaging manufacturing.

00:19:24.240 --> 00:19:27.620
Additionally, we will partner
with Scallion farmers in Fukaya,

00:19:27.620 --> 00:19:30.220
and a glass manufacturer in Saitama prefecture.

00:19:30.420 --> 00:19:33.560
Through environmental awareness
and supporting local business,

00:19:33.840 --> 00:19:38.780
we can hope to further improve
our company's public image.

00:19:38.780 --> 00:19:40.900
What about the costs?

00:19:41.240 --> 00:19:45.580
For all the work and money this will take,
are you even certain we can make a profit?

00:19:45.920 --> 00:19:50.920
Your fancy buzzwords are worthless
if they don't correspond to results.

00:19:51.280 --> 00:19:53.600
The demand must be nonexistent too.

00:19:54.820 --> 00:19:56.500
May I interject?

00:19:57.080 --> 00:20:02.300
I didn't ask for QA's opinion. Your job is to make
sure everything's safe and focus on the numbers.

00:20:02.820 --> 00:20:06.160
I see. If what you're looking for is numbers…

00:20:06.640 --> 00:20:12.910
89% of the participants at the tasting event
rated Scallion Ginger Ale positively.

00:20:14.360 --> 00:20:15.960
I believe that serves as proof.

00:20:17.260 --> 00:20:20.120
Well, we certainly can't ignore
the voices of our customers!

00:20:20.180 --> 00:20:22.880
That's it! We'll be proceeding
with Scallion Ginger Ale!

00:20:23.020 --> 00:20:23.880
Yes!

00:20:33.720 --> 00:20:35.000
Good work out there.

00:20:35.760 --> 00:20:40.400
Seems like Takeda got over his stage fright.
And you did a hell of a good job yourself.

00:20:40.600 --> 00:20:42.440
And you rocked that suit too.

00:20:42.840 --> 00:20:46.660
I'm so glad it all worked out
after everything we've been through.

00:20:47.180 --> 00:20:50.380
So? Don't you think this job
can be pretty fun sometimes?

00:20:51.420 --> 00:20:57.140
I mean, I got so many people involved, I just…
felt personally responsible, I guess.

00:20:57.620 --> 00:21:00.320
Hey! You saved our asses back there.

00:21:00.980 --> 00:21:06.900
I see Usuyama of the East is still great
at scoring when it matters most.

00:21:07.120 --> 00:21:11.660
Please. It's been years since I stopped playing.

00:21:12.220 --> 00:21:16.720
The years mean nothing when something's
so deeply ingrained in your soul.

00:21:18.820 --> 00:21:23.400
Usuyama. Are you sure you
don't want to play badminton again?

00:21:26.040 --> 00:21:27.100
I…

00:22:59.020 --> 00:23:02.880
[All-Japan Corporate Badminton Tournament]
[Day 4]

00:23:07.360 --> 00:23:09.020
How cute.

00:23:09.560 --> 00:23:12.450
All those losers lining up
to have their asses handed to them.
